<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tomás Guardia Gutiérrez</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1831">1831</a>–<a href="/years/1882">1882</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tomás Guardia Gutiérrez was a Costa Rican general who seized power in a coup in 1870 and dominated the country until his death in 1882. He issued the long-lasting constitution of 1871, abolished the death penalty in 1882 and began the railway to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> port of Limón. His authoritarian rule laid foundations of the liberal state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tomas-guardia-gutierrez.jpg" alt="Tomás Guardia Gutiérrez" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aquiles Bigot · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tom%C3%A1s_Guardia_Guti%C3%A9rrez.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
